Stage 1 evidence: standalone CMake/build passed; Qt6 `qmllint` passed; the offscreen harness started without diagnostics and exited via the bounded timeout (`124`); `git diff --check` passed. No Quickshell reload or live-shell action was performed. The scaffold reports no surface creation support and performs no Wayland operations.

Stage 2 ordering-only: the default-disabled standalone `SubsurfaceProbe` targets only its own harness `QWindow`, waits for visible/exposed lifecycle state with bounded single-shot retries, uses an isolated QtWayland private adapter, requests bounded synthetic magenta content below the parent by default or above it when explicitly selected, and fails closed offscreen/non-Wayland. It has no blur, screencopy, Quickshell internals, or production shell integration. Paired captures establish visual ordering: magenta is absent below the opaque parent and visible above it; protocol logs confirm matching requests with no errors. The lifecycle exercise then emitted `wl_surface#56.destroy()` without `wl_subsurface#46.destroy()` before a replacement child/parent commit; Hyprland PID 2558826 crashed in `CSubsurface::recheckDamageForSubsurfaces` and restarted safe mode. Treat missing explicit subsurface destruction as the leading client defect. Suspend live probes, fix teardown order, and verify only offline/offscreen. Above-parent is comparison-only, not a production recommendation.

Teardown fix: `WaylandSubsurfaceAdapter::destroy()` now destroys the `wl_subsurface` role before the child `wl_surface`, then releases the SHM wrapper and clears state. Offline build/static checks passed; compositor behavior remains unverified. Do not run the harness against a Wayland compositor.

Task 10 is complete as an offline/static-only verification boundary. Task 11 begins with a build-only `wayland-server` API sentinel; it creates no socket, display, protocol globals, or runtime side effect, and does not establish disposable-compositor containment.

Next evidence gate: offline hardening is complete, but compositor behavior remains unverified. Opt-in requires an affirmative value; lifecycle timers wait for observed `active`; initial/replacement/final-disable logs expose native child IDs; and native teardown logs retain IDs while destroying the role before the surface. `WAYLAND_DEBUG` remains authoritative for protocol ordering. A clean process exit without active-ID records and matching role-before-surface destroy ordering is insufficient evidence.

Disposable compositor gate: containment is fail-closed. Verified local help/static evidence requires bwrap 0.13.0 with mandatory `--unshare-all`, `--unshare-user`, `--unshare-ipc`, `--unshare-pid`, `--unshare-net`, `--unshare-cgroup`, `--clearenv`, private mounts, `--new-session`, `--die-with-parent`, and `--json-status-fd`; never use `*-try` flags because they continue without isolation. `systemd-run` offers `--property`, `--wait`, `--collect`, and documented resource properties, but effective user-manager enforcement and coredump suppression under this host's systemd-coredump pipe remain unverified. The actual containment launcher and runtime remain blocked pending authoritative verification of core suppression, identity cleanup, and post-client liveness. Installed Hyprland 0.56.2 hardcodes mandatory headless, optional DRM, and Wayland fallback implementations; no confirmed backend CLI selector exists. Aquamarine headless does not open a device itself, but startup still requires a render allocator unless NULL is first, and Hyprland does not request NULL. Do not expose `/dev/dri`, inherit the active `WAYLAND_DISPLAY`, or nest into the live desktop. Runtime validation remains blocked until an independently launched disposable outer compositor or separately built software/null allocator is available.

Upstream KWin v6.7.5 is not acceptable under the current no-device gate: `--virtual` selects `VirtualBackend`, creates `Session::Type::Noop`, and `VirtualBackend::initialize()` returns true with QPainter support, but `ApplicationWayland` calls `createGpuManager()` before backend selection. `GpuManager` opens `/dev/udmabuf`, creates a udev DRM monitor, and scans render devices, so the virtual backend does not provide the required no-device boundary.

The Qt-independent build-only fixture now proves scanner/protocol generation and public server linkage. It remains inert and unexecuted: it provides no server, compositor, CPU composition, or runtime containment, so it cannot prove visual ordering. Task 11 remains incomplete, and task 12 remains blocked.

Production boundary: no live shell integration, no compositor plugin, no screencopy, no fullscreen blur rule, and no production input/routing/focus/overlay/service changes. Production island fallback remains authoritative.
